      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we need to first find its prime factorization. We can see that 91 is divisible by 7, so we can write 91 as 7 x 13. Both 7 and 13 are prime numbers, so the prime factorization of 91 is 7 x 13.\n\nNow, we can use the formula for the sum of divisors of a number. If a number has the prime factorization $p_1^{a_1} p_2^{a_2} \\cdots p_n^{a_n}$, then the sum of its divisors is given by:\n\n$$(1 + p_1 + p_1^2 + \\cdots + p_1^{a_1})(1 + p_2 + p_2^2 + \\cdots + p_2^{a_2}) \\cdots (1 + p_n + p_n^2 + \\cdots + p_n^{a_n})$$\n\nIn our case, we have $91 = 7^1 \\times 13^1$, so the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is:\n\n$$(1 + 7)(1 + 13) = 8 \\times 14 = \\boxed{112}$$",
